  "summary": "Innovator in software development and applied artificial intelligence - work in natural language interface systems, machine learning, inference systems, knowledge representation, robust optimization, automatic markets for complex products, data-mining, model composition, text analysis, and fine-level and coarse-level parallel processing, and continual planning.  Recent work includes medical informatics, code search from unstructured text, traversal of medical ontologies, medical ASR and TTS.\n\nHave worked in Healthcare Informatics for the last decade, served as founder and visionary for several startup companies, participated in all aspects of software R&D and intellectual property creation, held positions including Chief Research Officer, Chief Science Officer, Chief Technical Officer, Project Lead, Systems Manager, and Systems Architect. Conducted team-building and project management for a range of projects performed on behalf of commercial and government customers. Chief technical author of seven Issued US patents.  Flexible and agile, capable of playing a wide variety of roles in companies of all sizes.\n\nTeaches University courses in Computer Science, and remains current in areas including machine learning,text analysis, agent-based programming, natural language processing, optimization, non-linear programming, computational intelligence, high-performance/massively parallel computing and rapid prototyping. Familiarity with adjacent fields including biomedical informatics, systems biology, operations research, quantitative financial modeling.\n\nSpecialties:\nNLP, Speech, Semantic Analysis of Documents\nKnowledge Discovery/Machine Learning, Deep Learning\n{non-linear,combinatorial} Optimization,  \nComputational Intelligence/Pragmatic Artificial Intelligence\n Intellectual Property Development\nComputer-enabled markets, Financial Modeling\nCoarse-Grained and fine-grained parallelism",
